---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
import VideoSection from '../../components/VideoSection.astro';
import { t } from '../../i18n/ui';
import type { Lang } from '../../i18n/utils';

const lang: Lang = 'en';
---
<Base lang={lang} path="/events/kvk/" title="Kingdom War (KvK): Survival &amp; Scoring" description="Server-versus-server war for the Royal City: the biweekly schedule, turret-first strategy for attackers, stall tactics for defenders, troop and resource risk, and the scoring overlap with Alliance Duel.">
  <GuidePage title="Kingdom War (KvK): Survival &amp; Scoring" description="Server-versus-server war for the Royal City: the biweekly schedule, turret-first strategy for attackers, stall tactics for defenders, troop and resource risk, and the scoring overlap with Alliance Duel." lang={lang}>
    <p>Kingdom War is the game&apos;s <strong>server-versus-server war</strong>: two kingdoms invade a shared map and fight over the <strong>Royal City</strong>. It runs <strong>biweekly</strong>, with scoring and preparation tasks through the week and the main battle condensed into a single window. Win by controlling the Royal City when the dust settles.</p>
    <p>This guide covers the schedule, attacker and defender strategy, universal rules, the mistakes that lose wars, and the economy rules that keep your account alive through it.</p>

    <h2 id="schedule">The Biweekly Schedule</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Preparation and scoring run through the week</strong> — the daily tasks and point categories build your kingdom&apos;s position before a single wall is contested.</li>
      <li><strong>The main battle is Saturday from reset</strong>, inside a <strong>4-hour window</strong>. That window is the whole war — everything before it is positioning.</li>
      <li><strong>Win condition: control the Royal City.</strong> Not most kills, not most points — who holds the city at the end.</li>
    </ul>
    <blockquote>Winning alliances aren&apos;t always the strongest — they&apos;re the most organized.</blockquote>

    <h2 id="attacker-playbook">Attacker Playbook</h2>
    <p>If your kingdom is on offense, the instinct is to rush the Royal City. That instinct loses wars.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Do not rush the city first.</strong> A direct push into the city runs into concentrated defense and turrets — it bleeds your strongest squads in the opening minutes.</li>
      <li><strong>Take the turrets first, then push.</strong> Every turret down widens your safe zone and strips the defenders&apos; map control before the city fight even begins.</li>
      <li><strong>Stay in rallies.</strong> Rallies are safer and stronger than solo marches — concentrated HP, concentrated buffs, and a march the defenders actually have to respect. The solo hero is the solo casualty.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="defender-playbook">Defender Playbook</h2>
    <p>Defenders are not trying to win a fight. Defenders are trying to <strong>run out a clock</strong>.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You need time, not kills.</strong> Every minute the attackers spend grinding through your defense is a minute they are not holding the city. Stalling is winning.</li>
      <li><strong>Reinforce constantly.</strong> Feed fresh squads into contested points as fast as they die. A point that never stops being defended eats the entire enemy window.</li>
      <li><strong>Rotate.</strong> Don&apos;t park everything on one lane — shift squads to wherever the pressure actually is, and make the attackers fight for every single inch of ground.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="universal-rules">Universal Rules</h2>
    <p>Whichever side you are on, the same rules apply:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Turrets first = map control.</strong> The turret line decides who moves safely. It is the first objective of the war, every time.</li>
      <li><strong>Never solo.</strong> Solo pushes are how accounts get deleted. March with rallies or not at all.</li>
      <li><strong>Reinforce constantly.</strong> Defense that stops receiving reinforcements falls in one wave.</li>
      <li><strong>Stay online the whole fight.</strong> The 4-hour window punishes anyone who logs off mid-war — your squads stay exactly where you left them, undefended.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="losing-mistakes">The Mistakes That Lose Wars</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Solo pushes</strong> — instant wipes that hand the enemy free kills and leave your alliance a squad short.</li>
      <li><strong>Ignoring turrets</strong> — attacking the city through intact turret lines is donating troops.</li>
      <li><strong>No reinforcement</strong> — a defense that stops rotating falls, then the next point falls, then the city falls.</li>
      <li><strong>Logging off mid-war</strong> — the 4-hour window does not pause for your schedule.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="economy-rules">KvK Economy: Troops, Resources, and Shields</h2>
    <p>Kingdom War is one of the few events with real account risk:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You CAN lose troops and resources when attacked</strong> — this is not a zero-risk event like <a href="/events/canyon/">Canyon Conquest</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Shield up</strong> during the war window. An unshielded city during KvK is a resource piñata for the enemy server.</li>
      <li><strong>Losses scale with your wall and research</strong> — a maxed wall and defensive research are what turn a massacre into a skirmish.</li>
      <li><strong>Save upgrades and speedups for the scoring days</strong> — the same double-value logic that governs <a href="/events/alliance-duel/">Alliance Duel</a> applies to KvK scoring tasks. Spending a big upgrade on a neutral day earns half.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="scoring-overlap">Scoring Overlap With Alliance Duel</h2>
    <p>KvK and Alliance Duel share scoring sources, and the community consensus is to exploit that every day:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Covert Ops and Caravans score for BOTH events.</strong> The same actions feed your duel total and your KvK total at once.</li>
      <li>That makes caravans a daily no-brainer — run them every single day of a duel week. The full caravan and plunder route is in the <a href="/events/wagon/">Guild Wagon &amp; Caravans guide</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The rest of the war economy — what to save, when to spend, which shop buys fund the war — is covered in the <a href="/economy/">Economy guide</a>.</p>

    <VideoSection topic="kvk" lang={lang} />
  </GuidePage>
</Base>
